# Content

When generating or editing content for the EA Belgium website, please follow these rules to ensure clarity, consistency, and alignment with our tone and style.

- Use a friendly and approachable tone, but avoid being too casual or chatty.
- Prefer simple and clear English. Assume your reader is smart but may be new to the topic.
- Use British spelling (e.g. “organise” not “organize”).
- Avoid em-dashes (—). Use commas or full stops instead.
- Use the European date format: day month year (e.g. 15 June 2025).
- Do not capitalise every word in titles. Use sentence case: ✅ “Join our events”, ❌ “Join Our Events”
- When referring to the movement, write effective altruism in lowercase (unless it's at the start of a sentence).
- When referring to the organisation, capitalise as Effective Altruism Belgium.
- Be precise and avoid jargon. If using a technical term or EA-specific concept, consider linking to a brief explanation or providing one in the text.
- Write clear calls to action (e.g. “Sign up for our newsletter” or “Get involved”).
